SUMMARY:The Helpers — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: The Helpers\nRuntime: 80 min\nDirector: Peter Wayne\nGen
 re: Documentary\n\nEmbedding directly within five active warzones\, this ur
 gent hybrid documentary blends raw frontline footage with stunning 2D anima
 tion to follow the humanitarian heroes risking everything for strangers. Tr
 ansforming the testimonies of 100 refugees and aid workers into a global ca
 ll to action\, the film operates as a 100% non-profit rescue mission engine
 ered to secure vital aid for half a million people a year before time runs 
 out.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768517
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tmdb:1768486
DTSTAMP:20260914T191029Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Mushroom Cloud: A Hibakusha Story — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Mushroom Cloud: A Hibakusha Story\nRuntime: 98 min\nDire
 ctor: James Medina\nGenre: Documentary\n\nThe documentary portrays the afte
 rmath of atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. Through the voices of H
 ibakusha—atomic bomb survivors—the film transforms history into memories of
  devastation\, trauma\, and survival. Hidankyo officers: Michiko Kodama\, T
 erumi Tanaka\, Jiro Hamasumi\, and Toshiko Hamanaka reveal enduring physica
 l and emotional scars\, as well as discrimination. They describe the politi
 cal and international obstacles that shaped efforts to support atomic bomb 
 victims and abolish nuclear weapons. The narrative explores the pivotal 195
 4 Bikini Atoll Incident\, which broke the silence and led to Hidankyo’s fou
 nding in 1956\, with members attending UN conferences to advocate for peace
 . Professor Peter Kuznick discusses how Eisenhower and many military leader
 s considered the bombings unnecessary\, as Japan had already surrendered. H
 e provides context on nuclear diplomacy\, failure of the NPT and persistenc
 e of nine nuclear powers.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768486
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tmdb:1768463
DTSTAMP:20260914T191029Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Ganj\, The Treasures of Shah Jo Risalo — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Ganj\, The Treasures of Shah Jo Risalo\nRuntime: 75 min\
 nDirector: Shamim Junejo\nGenre: Documentary\n\nGANJ: The Treasures of Shah
  Jo Risalo explores the timeless wisdom of Shah Abdul Latif Bhittai a Sufi 
 poet\, saint and philosopher. Through the lens of his poetic works referred
  to as the Shah Jo Risalo\, the film retells the harrowing tales of Bhittai
 ’s Seven Queens: Marvi\, Moomal\, Sohni\, Leela\, Noori\, Sassi\, and Sorat
 h. Written nearly 350 years ago\, these stories remarkably challenge patria
 rchal notions by portraying women as self determined\, and devoted seekers 
 of justice. Featuring analysis from renowned experts and poetry sung by the
  legendary Abida Parveen\, GANJ seeks to globalise Shah Abdul Latif Bhittai
 ’s legacy and firmly establish him as the first known feminist Sufi poet in
  the world. The title GANJ\, meaning bountiful or plenty\, aptly suggests t
 hat the wisdom found in Shah Jo Risalo are treasures waiting to be uncovere
 d and the messages of courage\, spirituality and love remain profoundly rel
 evant today.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768463
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tmdb:1768283
DTSTAMP:20260914T191029Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Son of The Steppe — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Son of The Steppe\nRuntime: 100 min\nDirector: Tao Hu\nG
 enre: Drama\n\nIn the 1970s\, Tyn Bator left Hohhot for the remote steppes 
 of Inner Mongolia. He revived a failing milk powder factory and received a 
 promotion. After many educated young people returned to the cities\, he mar
 ried a local woman and stayed. When local herders questioned the effectiven
 ess of rotational grazing\, he took over the worst pasture. Within a year\,
  he achieved tremendous progress\, helping to spread scientific livestock f
 arming methods. He put down roots in the steppes and devoted himself wholeh
 eartedly to serving the local population.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768283
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tmdb:1768262
DTSTAMP:20260914T191029Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Mysteries of Lake Brosno — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Mysteries of Lake Brosno\nRuntime: 105 min\nDirector: Se
 rgey Ohotin\nGenre: Drama\, Romance\, Fantasy\n\nAfter her mother's death\,
  Masha and her father\, a priest\, move to Lake Brosno\, shrouded in the le
 gend of an ancient lizard. There\, she meets scientist Nikolai and his fath
 er\, Igor\, obsessed with finding the mythical lizard. Nikolai's experiment
  with infrasound sonar spirals out of control\, killing Igor and Masha\, wh
 o was trying to save her lover. Having lost Masha\, Nikolai discovers faith
 —will he be able to resist death?
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768262
END:VEVENT
