SUMMARY:Chernobyl-2: Life After — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Chernobyl-2: Life After\nRuntime: 67 min\nDirector: Olga
  Antimony\nGenre: Documentary\n\nThirty years ago\, a little girl watched h
 er parents’ wedding\, remembering the lilies in her mother’s hands. Today\,
  she is getting married herself in Dnipro\, a Ukrainian city living through
  years of war and air raid sirens. Katya’s father was a liquidator of the C
 hernobyl nuclear disaster. He called himself and his friends “larks” — bird
 s that are the first to rise into the spring sky — and called his struggle 
 to survive after the catastrophe “Chernobyl-2.” In 2022\, a new catastrophe
  enters the lives of his wife Tanya and daughter Katya: Russia’s full-scale
  invasion of Ukraine. Combining archival footage filmed more than twenty ye
 ars ago with material shot during the current war\, Chernobyl-2: Life After
  traces how one catastrophe echoes through another — and how a family livin
 g in the shadow of Chernobyl and war continues to love\, laugh\, endure\, a
 nd move forward.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1768432
END:VEVENT
