SUMMARY:Darkhan — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: Darkhan\nRuntime: 38 min\nDirector: Vladimir Ponomarev\,
  Alexey Lagerev\, Daniil Balushkin\nGenre: Documentary\n\nIn the mountains 
 of the Eastern Sayan range\, in the south-west of the Republic of Buryatia\
 , lies the ulus of Myla. Life here is a constant struggle. From something a
 s basic as heating one's home\, the struggle extends to every aspect of lif
 e in this small Khamnigan settlement. How do Darkhan's creativity\, inquisi
 tive mind\, and gifted hands help the entire ulus survive in the harsh cond
 itions of Zakamna? And what philosophy allows Dondok Dorzhiyevich to reconc
 ile the seemingly irreconcilable - being both a darkhan and a shaman who cr
 eates Buddhist ritual objects?
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1763976
END:VEVENT
